Prompt:
Why is the 16S rRNA gene specifically targeted for identifying unknown bacteria?
AI reply (summary):
Explained conserved regions for universal primers and hypervariable regions (V1–V9) that distinguish species; noted widespread use in clinical and environmental microbiology.
