Prompt 12 – Local vs Global Alignment
Prompt:
Why is local alignment (BLAST) preferred over global alignment (Needleman–Wunsch) for short DNA queries?
AI reply (summary):
Clarified that short reads usually match only part of a long reference genome; local alignment finds the best matching region without forcing end-to-end alignment.
